  "findings": [
    "Default -1 participated in v2 profiling, won seeds18/19, and survived each corresponding fresh warm file reload as a genuine hit.",
    "Natural warm v2/v1 median paired latency ratios are0.9902773854189744 eager and1.0142401094145443 graph; results do not establish uniform v2 superiority.",
    "Measured warm eager selected-to-best oracle ratios have median1.0045476697508253 for v1 and1.0200070984364933 for v2. Natural latency and candidate-quality measurements answer different questions.",
    "Untuned natural default is a true lookup miss, whereas tuned cold/warm winners use memory/file hits. The roughly49.5us untuned eager versus40\u201343us cached eager gap includes lookup/dispatch path differences and cannot be attributed solely to different GPU algorithms.",
    "Cold startup remains a secondary diagnostic; no model startup or serving-throughput claim is made."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Three fresh-worker trials, not45 independent trials; fifteen samples estimate each worker's latency.",
    "Taking the minimum of nine noisy candidate estimates makes the measured oracle optimistic. Small apparent regret includes minimum-selection noise, execution order, clock and sampling variation; no confidence interval or significance claim is established.",
    "Regret uses selected-versus-best within the same sweep and tier. Natural-versus-oracle timing compares separate windows and may be below1; it is not pure selection regret.",
    "Default natural miss timing is deliberately separate from cached-default oracle timing.",
    "This tests one shape on an experimental source overlay and one H100 NVL, with no distributed, BF16, managed-store, explicit-policy or full-model qualification.",
    "M144 is still pending; no result-dependent change to its preregistered execution is proposed."
  ],
